4. Commercial Use: 1% Royalty

   You may create and distribute a Commercial Product only if You pay the
   Licensor a royalty of one percent (1%) of all Gross Revenue from that
   Commercial Product, under these terms:

   a. Notice. Before the first sale or subscription, You notify the Licensor
      through https://github.com/Defectuous (for example by opening an issue in
      the AlpacaTools repository) that You intend to offer a Commercial
      Product, and agree a payment method with the Licensor.

   b. Payment. Royalties are calculated and paid each calendar quarter, within
      thirty (30) days after the end of the quarter.

   c. Reporting. Each payment is accompanied by a statement of Gross Revenue
      for that quarter.

   d. Records. You keep accurate records of Gross Revenue for at least three
      (3) years and make them available to the Licensor, or to an independent
      accountant it chooses, on reasonable request, no more than once a year.

   e. Duration. The royalty applies for as long as the Commercial Product
      incorporates or is derived from the Software.

   The Licensor may agree different commercial terms in a separate written
   agreement, which then takes precedence over this section.

